diff --git a/docs/whats_new_in_3_3.rst b/docs/whats_new_in_3_3.rst
index 3e06c63..752b032 100644
--- a/docs/whats_new_in_3_3.rst
+++ b/docs/whats_new_in_3_3.rst
@@ -100,6 +100,16 @@ Fixed Bugs
 - Fixed minor formatting issues in ``pyparsing.testing.with_line_numbers`` discovered
   while developing the TINY language example.
 
+- ``QuotedString`` no longer strips white space from ``quote_char`` and
+  ``end_quote_char``. White space in the quote chars is now significant and must be
+  matched in the input string, so quote chars such as ``"\n;"`` work as written
+  (previously the newline was silently dropped, leaving a ``";"``-delimited string).
+  If ``quote_char`` starts with white space, those characters are dropped from the
+  expression's skippable white space so the opening quote can still be matched. Quote
+  chars consisting only of white space continue to raise ``ValueError``. This is a
+  potentially breaking change for parsers that passed quote chars with surrounding
+  white space and relied on it being stripped.
+
 - ``DelimitedList`` and ``nested_expr`` now auto-suppress delimiting commas when the
   delimiter is already a ``Suppress``; this avoids the need for extra wrapping.
 
